{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2247","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2247","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2247\",\"parent_revision\":\"d38ac2ee74f351fdee917bb1d1a6473adbe5e170355fdba2093b9e03eda828ca\",\"root_revision\":\"d38ac2ee74f351fdee917bb1d1a6473adbe5e170355fdba2093b9e03eda828ca\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nIn multi-agent workflows where several spawned agents each ensure `gh` is installed (per the `/gh` skill's standard activation pattern documented in CLAUDE.md `<gh_cli_usage>`), every agent re-fetches identical release metadata.\\n\\n- Anonymous rate limit is 60 requests/hour (per the research entry's caveat #5 at line 215 of ./research/developer-tools/gh-skill.md)\\n- With `GITHUB_TOKEN` the limit is 5000/hour but each call still adds latency\\n- Multi-agent setup time scales linearly with agent count rather than being amortized\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **setup_gh.py re-fetches github release metadata on every invocation \u2014 no local cache** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/developer-tools/gh-skill.md \u2014 pattern: Cached metadata (Integration Opportunities)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-10\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`./.claude/skills/gh/scripts/setup_gh.py` `fetch_latest_release()` (lines 230-279) issues an unconditional HTTPS GET to `https://api.github.com/repos/cli/cli/releases/latest` on every invocation. `fetch_checksums()` (lines 320-354) issues a second HTTPS GET for the checksums asset. There is no cache lookup before these calls.\\n\\nVerification on 2026-05-10: grep of `setup_gh.py` for `cache`, `json.load`, `TTL`, `expir` returns only one match (a docstring mention of \\\"expired token\\\"). No cache implementation exists.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Where Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `./.claude/skills/gh/scripts/setup_gh.py` lines 230-279 \u2014 `fetch_latest_release()` always calls the API\\n- `./.claude/skills/gh/scripts/setup_gh.py` lines 320-354 \u2014 `fetch_checksums()` always downloads the checksums asset\\n- The script's existing short-circuit at lines 730-735 (skip install if installed version matches latest) requires the network call to determine \\\"latest\\\" \u2014 so it does not avoid the API hit\\n</div>\\n\\n## User Provided Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry `./research/developer-tools/gh-skill.md` Integration Opportunities section line 239 suggests: \\\"Cache GitHub release information (version, checksums) locally to reduce API calls during multi-agent workflows\\\". This is preserved as context, not a requirement \u2014 the cache TTL, location, and invalidation policy are for grooming/planning to determine.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Source\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nResearch entry: ./research/developer-tools/gh-skill.md \u2014 pattern: Cached metadata (Integration Opportunities)\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b8785d90219779f43a8d3a9e25df0803f537b420e7ef585e733795c22e5d2eb7\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCUCcQ\"}"}